WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.400
( theme music playing)

2
00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:50.480
( crickets chirping )

3
00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:54.600
( animal calls )

4
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.440
( grunts )

5
00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.800
( muffled grunting )

6
00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:32.320
( muffled shout )

7
00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.120
( grunts )

8
00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.120
( wood creaking )

9
00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:57.120
-( men shouting )
-( seagulls screeching )

10
00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:06.800
Is that Estermont?

11
00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:09.040
Tarth. Ser Jaime.

12
00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.040
The Sapphire Isle.

13
00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.720
Why are we on
a merchant ship?

14
00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.400
Why no Lannister sails?

15
00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.960
This ship's sailing
to Oldtown.

16
00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:27.520
We'll get off earlier 
not far from Sunspear.

17
00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.800
row ourselves
to the Dornish shore in the night.

18
00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:32.880
You ever been to Dorne?

19
00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.640
-No.
-I have.

20
00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:36.360
The Dornish are crazy.

21
00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.400
All they want to do
is fight and fuck. fuck and fight.

22
00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:41.160
You should be happy
to go back.

23
00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:44.080
There's nothing
like a good fight

24
00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.320
to get you in the mood
for fucking.

25
00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.360
And there's nothing like
a fuck-mad Dornish girl

26
00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.640
to clear your head
for the next fight.

27
00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:52.720
It's how the two
work together.

28
00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.800
Now we're gonna be doing
a lot of fighting. I'm sure.

29
00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.480
Well. I am.

30
00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.080
But I don't imagine we'll get
to stick around for the rest.

31
00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:01.080
Not after we've kidnapped
their princess.

32
00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:02.960
We're not kidnapping
their princess.

33
00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:05.920
We're rescuing my niece.
bringing her back to her family.

34
00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:07.400
Your niece?

35
00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:17.280
I've been doing this sort of thing
a long time.

36
00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.120
-I'm good at it.
-That's why you're here.

37
00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.440
I know.
Why are you here?

38
00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.600
Why not send 40 of me?
Or an army?

39
00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:25.960
Unlike most folks.
you've actually got one.

40
00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:28.800
Because I don't want
to start a war.

41
00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:31.880
That still doesn't explain
what you're doing here.

42
00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:36.040
It has to be me.

43
00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.720
If I'm putting
something like this together.

44
00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.600
a one-handed man
who happens to be

45
00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.160
one of the most recognizable
faces in Westeros is not--

46
00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.000
It has to be me.

47
00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:54.720
You set your brother
free. didn't you?

48
00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.920
I'll bet your sister
didn't like that.

49
00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.760
Varys set him free.

50
00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:11.440
Well. if you ever see
the wee fucker.

51
00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:12.960
give him my regards.

52
00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.840
He murdered my father.

53
00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:24.320
If I ever see him.
I'll split him in two.

54
00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:27.600
And then I'll give
him your regards.

55
00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:38.080
The Iron Bank has called
in one-tenth of the crown's debts.

56
00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:40.720
Given the expense
of rebuilding the royal fleet--

57
00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:43.600
-How much can the crown afford?
-With winter coming.

58
00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:46.800
half what they ask.
less?

59
00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:49.920
You're the Master of Coin.
How do we pay them?

60
00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:52.000
House Tyrell could
front the gold

61
00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:54.040
and the crown would
pay us back in time

62
00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.560
or I'd have words
with my daughter.

63
00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:04.120
You've already
given us too much.

64
00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:08.040
No. we must arrange
better terms with the Iron Bank.

65
00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.440
-Absolutely.
-In person.

66
00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:13.600
-Me?
-We must send

67
00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:15.080
an envoy to the Iron Bank.

68
00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:18.480
someone of importance to show
these bankers our respect.

69
00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:21.520
As the king's Master of Coin.
I can think of no one more qualified.

70
00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:23.400
I would be honored.
Your Grace.

71
00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.240
The king's expressed concern
about his father-in-law's

72
00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.200
safety on this voyage.

73
00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:34.480
He's ordered Ser Meryn to personally
lead your escort.

74
00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.160
My very own
Kingsguard?

75
00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:40.160
-Please express my--
-Safe travels. Lord Tyrell.

76
00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:42.080
Of course.
Of course.

77
00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:45.800
I'll give your regards
to the Titan of Braavos.

78
00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:47.560
( laughs )

79
00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:57.440
The small council grows
smaller and smaller.

80
00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.680
Not small enough.

81
00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:12.440
Cersei: May I offer you some wine.
Your Holiness?

82
00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:14.280
No.

83
00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:20.200
The old High Septon
would have asked the vintage.

84
00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:23.040
I could say that our minds
are temples to the Seven

85
00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.560
and should be kept pure.

86
00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:28.680
But the truth is
I don't like the taste.

87
00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.760
Hmm.

88
00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:33.000
How may I serve?

89
00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:37.760
All over Westeros
we hear of septs being burned.

90
00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:40.760
Silent Sisters raped.

91
00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:43.280
bodies of holy men
piled in the streets.

92
00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.800
Wars teach people
to obey the sword. not the gods.

93
00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:49.760
Perhaps the gods
need a sword of their own.

94
00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:51.560
In the days before
the Targaryens.

95
00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:54.840
the Faith Militant dispensed
the justice of the Seven.

96
00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:59.120
Well. the Faith Militant was disarmed
more than two centuries ago.

97
00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:02.680
If I explain their holy purpose
to my son the king.

98
00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:04.760
I have no doubt
he will sign a decree

99
00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.800
arming the believers
you felt worthy.

100
00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:11.120
An army that defends the bodies
and souls of the common people?

101
00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:14.080
An army in service
to the gods themselves.

102
00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:16.160
And to you. of course.

103
00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:18.240
as the chosen representative
of the Seven.

104
00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:20.800
An honor I never expected.

105
00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:22.560
Or. indeed.
ever wished for.

106
00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:24.240
Which is why
you were chosen.

107
00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:28.480
You and I both know
how the world works.

108
00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:30.720
Too often the wicked
are the wealthiest.

109
00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:32.400
beyond the reach
of justice.

110
00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:36.080
The king himself cannot always punish
those who deserve it most.

111
00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:39.040
All sinners are equal
before the gods.

112
00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:47.400
What would you say if I told you of a
great sinner in our very midst?

113
00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:50.160
Shielded by gold
and privilege.

114
00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:54.600
May the Father
judge him justly.

115
00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:59.720
( merchants shouting )

116
00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:07.000
( grunts )

117
00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:09.160
( people screaming )

118
00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:17.840
( muffled groaning )

119
00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:28.160
-( grunting )
-What are you doing?

120
00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:31.520
( man grunts )

121
00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:33.800
Help me!
Help me!

122
00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:42.720
-( moans )
-Yeah. Yeah.

123
00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:45.040
( screams )
Get off me!

124
00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:48.200
( grunts )

125
00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.480
-Come on.
-( women shriek )

126
00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:55.880
Shut up!
Move!

127
00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:57.880
( women screaming )

128
00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:05.040
This is Lord Petyr Baelish's
establishment.

129
00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:06.520
( grunts )

130
00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:12.560
( man screams )

131
00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:18.640
-( man screams )
-Faith Militant: Cocksuckers.

132
00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:20.960
Boy fucker.

133
00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:23.760
You buggering filth!

134
00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:27.080
There's a special place
in the seventh hell for your kind.

135
00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:29.760
Man: Please.
Please. I'll pay.

136
00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:31.640
I'll--I'll pay
all of you.

137
00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:33.640
Yes. you will.

138
00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:38.680
( man screams )

139
00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:48.280
( panting )

140
00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:56.480
( grunting )

141
00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:04.080
( applause )

142
00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:09.280
Seize him.

143
00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:10.880
-Sinner.
-( grunting )

144
00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:13.520
-Loras: Get your hands off me.
-Ser Loras of House Tyrell.

145
00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:15.520
you have broken the laws
of gods and men.

146
00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:18.200
Who do you
think you are?

147
00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:20.960
Justice.

148
00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:29.480
Why is my brother
in a cell?

149
00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:31.920
I-I don't know.

150
00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:33.520
I-I didn't order it.

151
00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:35.920
We both know who did.

152
00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:39.680
You told me she was returning
to Casterly Rock.

153
00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.960
Are you saying
my mother's behind this?

154
00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:44.400
She's jealous
you're not hers anymore.

155
00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:47.200
Arresting my brother
is her revenge.

156
00:11:47.360 --> 00:11:49.200
Aren't you and Mother
getting along?

157
00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:51.160
( huffs )

158
00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:58.240
Oh. my sweet.
sweet king.

159
00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:02.840
Do you have any affection
for me at all?

160
00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:06.240
Of course I do.

161
00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:08.120
You're my queen.

162
00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:10.400
I can't bear
to think of my brother

163
00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:13.040
locked away
in some grimy cell.

164
00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:17.280
I'll set him free
for you.

165
00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:18.800
Do you promise?

166
00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:27.880
I demand that
Ser Loras be freed now.

167
00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:29.680
Did I arrest him?

168
00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:33.320
Well. no.

169
00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:35.720
But y-you armed
the Faith Militant.

170
00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:39.040
You gave the High Sparrow
an army.

171
00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:41.400
I did.

172
00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:45.280
And your wife has
every right to criticize.

173
00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:47.880
We can't allow fanatics
to arrest the queen's brother

174
00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:50.360
no matter his perversions.

175
00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:52.120
Then...

176
00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:56.120
can I tell Margaery
you'll have Ser Loras released?

177
00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:58.680
I told you.
I'm not holding Ser Loras.

178
00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:00.600
You're the king.

179
00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:02.360
I'm sure if you speak
to the High Sparrow.

180
00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:04.720
he'll release
the poor boy.

181
00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:11.240
Halt!

182
00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:21.400
( coughing. chatter )

183
00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:36.120
His Holiness is praying.
He will not be disturbed.

184
00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:40.800
Give the order
and we'll clear out this rabble.

185
00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:44.920
You mean. kill them?

186
00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:46.840
Here at the sept?

187
00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:48.760
You'd be sending them
to meet the gods that they love.

188
00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:54.600
Man:
Bastard!

189
00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:56.720
Man #2:
You're an abomination!

190
00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:03.800
Man #3:
Born of sin!

191
00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:05.880
Woman:
Filthy bastard!

192
00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:12.560
We'll find another way.

193
00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:16.160
Man #4:
Abomination!

194
00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:23.560
My queen?

195
00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:30.760
There was no way
to free Ser Loras without violence.

196
00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:36.360
You're the King
of the Andals.

197
00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:38.040
the Lord
of the Seven Kingdoms.

198
00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:40.080
the Protector
of the Realm.

199
00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:43.200
and you let a band of fanatics
imprison your brother by law.

200
00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:46.280
I'm going to speak
with the High Sparrow.

201
00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:48.080
Are you?
When?

202
00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:52.080
-I-I don't know.
-You don't know?

203
00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:54.400
He was praying
just now.

204
00:14:57.360 --> 00:14:59.080
I have to send word
to Grandmother.

205
00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:02.320
Will you
come back later?

206
00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:06.440
I need to be with
my family. Your Grace.

207
00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:09.400
Of course.

208
00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:12.160
( grunting )

209
00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:13.840
Selyse:
You think highly of this boy?

210
00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:15.360
Good.

211
00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:17.240
Stannis: Lord Commander
of the Night's Watch.

212
00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:19.920
And a bastard
by some tavern slut.

213
00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:22.840
Perhaps. but that wasn't
Ned Stark's way.

214
00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:28.360
I should have
given you a son.

215
00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:31.560
Not your fault.

216
00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:33.520
Whose. then?

217
00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:35.840
I gave you nothing
but weakness.

218
00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:40.080
And deformity.

219
00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:43.960
Those scars mean nothing
to the Lord of Light.

220
00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:45.960
My lady.

221
00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:48.600
Her father is the Lord's
chosen king.

222
00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:51.160
and her father's blood
runs through her veins.

223
00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:02.080
You march on
Winterfell soon?

224
00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:05.240
We must
to beat the snows.

225
00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:08.800
Once before. you put
your faith in Ser Davos

226
00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:10.760
and left me behind.

227
00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:15.160
I hope you won't make
that mistake again.

228
00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:16.760
I won't.

229
00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:20.800
I need you.

230
00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:23.200
You only need faith.
my king.

231
00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:29.440
And you. my lady.
what do you need?

232
00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:33.880
To serve my Lord.

233
00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:36.080
( grunting )

234
00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:39.880
Lord Ashford.

235
00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:47.080
Lady Caulfield.

236
00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:51.240
Oh. Lord Smallwood.

237
00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:53.040
I've never even heard
of these people.

238
00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:55.400
They haven't heard
of you. either.

239
00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:57.720
But we need men
and they have some.

240
00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:02.720
How many men does this
Lord Mayzen have to send us?

241
00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:04.960
More than Lord Wibberley.

242
00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:20.160
-Not him.
-I know. I'm sorry.

243
00:17:20.320 --> 00:17:22.360
But we need men
and supplies

244
00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:23.880
and Roose Bolton's
the Warden of the North.

245
00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:26.040
-He murdered my brother.
-We swore to be

246
00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:28.360
the watchers on the Wall.

247
00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:31.760
We can't watch the Wall
with 50 men.

248
00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:33.560
And we can't get more men

249
00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:35.640
without help from
the Warden of the North.

250
00:17:57.600 --> 00:17:59.680
Apologies. my lady.

251
00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:09.360
( door closes )

252
00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:12.760
Lord Commander.

253
00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:15.160
How can I help you?

254
00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:17.240
Come with us
when we ride south.

255
00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:20.400
None of us know the castle
as well as you do.

256
00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:22.840
Its hidden tunnels.
its weaknesses.

257
00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:25.360
its people.

258
00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:27.560
Winterfell
was your home once.

259
00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:31.400
Don't you want
to chase the rats out of it?

260
00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:36.360
Castle Black
is my home now.

261
00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:39.800
The Night's Watch take no part in the
wars of the Seven Kingdoms.

262
00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:41.760
There's only one war.

263
00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:43.920
Life against death.

264
00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:48.800
Come. let me show you
what you're fighting for.

265
00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:51.480
You're gonna show me
some vision in the fire?

266
00:18:51.640 --> 00:18:54.760
Forgive me. my lady.
I don't trust in visions.

267
00:18:56.120 --> 00:18:59.480
No visions.
No magic.

268
00:18:59.640 --> 00:19:01.440
Just life.

269
00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:22.920
Do you feel
my heart beating?

270
00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:27.160
There's power in you.

271
00:19:27.320 --> 00:19:29.880
You resist it.
and that's your mistake.

272
00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:31.640
Embrace it.

273
00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:45.080
The Lord of Light
made us male and female.

274
00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:47.480
Two parts
of a greater whole.

275
00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:52.080
In our joining.
there's power.

276
00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:54.560
Power to make life.

277
00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:56.840
power to make light.

278
00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:59.680
and power
to cast shadows.

279
00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:02.560
I don't think Stannis
would like that very much.

280
00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:05.680
Then we shouldn't
tell him.

281
00:20:06.880 --> 00:20:09.080
-I can't.
-Why?

282
00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:12.280
I swore a vow.

283
00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:15.840
I loved another.

284
00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:18.040
The dead
don't need lovers.

285
00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:20.160
Only the living.

286
00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:27.200
I know.

287
00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:29.160
But I still love her.

288
00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:45.520
You know nothing.
Jon Snow.

289
00:20:58.720 --> 00:21:00.480
( knocks on door )

290
00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:22.720
Are you lonely?

291
00:21:24.320 --> 00:21:25.640
Just bored.

292
00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:27.280
My father used
to tell me that boredom

293
00:21:27.440 --> 00:21:28.960
indicates a lack
of inner resources.

294
00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:30.560
Were you bored
a lot. too?

295
00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:33.000
I know
Castle Black

296
00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:34.560
is no place
for a child. but--

297
00:21:34.720 --> 00:21:37.880
I like it.
I thought I'd be left at home.

298
00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:40.360
I know Mother
didn't want to bring me.

299
00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:42.360
Why do you say that?

300
00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:46.040
She told me.
"I don't want to bring you."

301
00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:49.440
She shouldn't 
have said that.

302
00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:01.000
Are you ashamed
of me. Father?

303
00:22:11.840 --> 00:22:14.280
When you were an infant.

304
00:22:14.440 --> 00:22:17.720
a Dornish trader
landed on Dragonstone.

305
00:22:17.880 --> 00:22:20.920
His goods were junk
except for one wooden doll.

306
00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:25.760
He had even sewn a dress
on it in the colors of our house.

307
00:22:27.520 --> 00:22:29.680
No doubt he had
heard of your birth

308
00:22:29.840 --> 00:22:32.760
and assumed new fathers
were easy targets.

309
00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:39.320
I still remember how you smiled
when I put that doll in your cradle.

310
00:22:40.800 --> 00:22:43.040
How you pressed it
to your cheek.

311
00:22:49.840 --> 00:22:52.080
By the time we burned the doll.
it was too late.

312
00:22:54.760 --> 00:22:56.880
I was told you would die.

313
00:22:57.040 --> 00:22:59.760
Or worse.

314
00:22:59.920 --> 00:23:01.720
the greyscale
would go slow.

315
00:23:01.880 --> 00:23:04.720
Let you grow just enough
to know the world

316
00:23:04.880 --> 00:23:06.760
before taking it
away from you.

317
00:23:06.920 --> 00:23:09.360
Everyone advised me to send
you to the ruins of Valyria

318
00:23:09.520 --> 00:23:11.480
to live out your short life
with the Stone Men

319
00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:14.280
before the sickness
spread through the castle.

320
00:23:15.720 --> 00:23:18.160
I told them all
to go to hell.

321
00:23:19.680 --> 00:23:22.520
I called in every maester
on this side of the world.

322
00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:25.560
Every healer.
Every apothecary.

323
00:23:27.640 --> 00:23:29.640
They stopped the disease
and saved your life.

324
00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:32.560
'Cause you did not belong
across the world

325
00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:35.320
with the bloody Stone Men.

326
00:23:35.480 --> 00:23:38.000
You are the Princess Shireen
of House Baratheon.

327
00:23:40.600 --> 00:23:42.240
And you are my daughter.

328
00:23:58.480 --> 00:24:00.680
( water dripping )

329
00:24:41.280 --> 00:24:43.320
Littlefinger: I thought I might
find you here.

330
00:24:45.880 --> 00:24:47.760
Your Aunt Lyanna.

331
00:24:47.920 --> 00:24:50.440
Father never
talked about her.

332
00:24:52.160 --> 00:24:54.880
Sometimes I'd find him
down here lighting the candles.

333
00:24:56.320 --> 00:24:57.840
They say
she was beautiful.

334
00:24:58.000 --> 00:25:00.200
I saw her once.

335
00:25:00.360 --> 00:25:03.040
I was a boy living
with your mother's family.

336
00:25:03.200 --> 00:25:06.680
Lord Whent held
a great tourney at Harrenhal.

337
00:25:06.840 --> 00:25:08.680
Everyone was there.

338
00:25:08.840 --> 00:25:12.000
The Mad King.
your father.

339
00:25:12.160 --> 00:25:13.520
Robert Baratheon.

340
00:25:13.680 --> 00:25:15.360
and Lyanna.

341
00:25:15.520 --> 00:25:18.120
She was already
promised to Robert.

342
00:25:18.280 --> 00:25:19.880
You can imagine
what it was like for me.

343
00:25:20.040 --> 00:25:23.360
a boy from nowhere
with nothing to his name.

344
00:25:23.520 --> 00:25:25.120
watching these
legendary men

345
00:25:25.280 --> 00:25:27.880
tilting
at the lists.

346
00:25:28.040 --> 00:25:30.720
The last two riders
were Barristan Selmy

347
00:25:30.880 --> 00:25:32.680
and Rhaegar Targaryen.

348
00:25:32.840 --> 00:25:36.320
When Rhaegar won.
everyone cheered for their prince.

349
00:25:36.480 --> 00:25:38.240
I remember the girls laughing
when he took off his helmet

350
00:25:38.400 --> 00:25:40.200
and they saw
that silver hair.

351
00:25:40.360 --> 00:25:42.480
How handsome he was.

352
00:25:42.640 --> 00:25:45.200
Until he rode
right past his wife.

353
00:25:45.360 --> 00:25:47.160
Elia Martell.

354
00:25:47.320 --> 00:25:48.960
and all the smiles died.

355
00:25:50.280 --> 00:25:52.480
I've never seen
so many people so quiet.

356
00:25:53.600 --> 00:25:56.840
He rode past his wife

357
00:25:57.000 --> 00:26:00.600
and he lay a crown
of winter roses in Lyanna's lap.

358
00:26:00.760 --> 00:26:02.640
Blue as frost.

359
00:26:05.880 --> 00:26:07.920
How many tens of thousands
had to die

360
00:26:08.080 --> 00:26:09.800
because Rhaegar
chose your aunt?

361
00:26:12.160 --> 00:26:14.960
Yes. he chose her.

362
00:26:15.120 --> 00:26:17.360
And then he kidnapped her
and raped her.

363
00:26:25.120 --> 00:26:27.080
Come.

364
00:26:27.240 --> 00:26:29.320
Let's speak somewhere
the dead can't hear us.

365
00:26:34.360 --> 00:26:35.920
You're dressed
for riding.

366
00:26:36.080 --> 00:26:38.360
I am.

367
00:26:38.520 --> 00:26:40.200
Where are you going?

368
00:26:40.360 --> 00:26:42.120
King's Landing.

369
00:26:42.280 --> 00:26:43.920
King's Landing?

370
00:26:44.080 --> 00:26:45.840
Cersei sent for me.

371
00:26:46.000 --> 00:26:48.400
We mustn't let her
sniff out any trouble.

372
00:26:48.560 --> 00:26:50.160
You can't leave me here.

373
00:26:50.320 --> 00:26:52.520
I know how hard it is to live with
people you despise.

374
00:26:52.680 --> 00:26:54.160
Believe me.

375
00:26:54.320 --> 00:26:56.040
But it won't be for long.

376
00:26:56.200 --> 00:26:57.520
How do you know?

377
00:26:58.920 --> 00:27:01.960
Stannis Baratheon
garrisons at Castle Black.

378
00:27:02.120 --> 00:27:04.280
He'll march south
to King's Landing

379
00:27:04.440 --> 00:27:06.200
before the winter snows
block his way.

380
00:27:06.360 --> 00:27:09.120
But first he has
to take Winterfell.

381
00:27:09.280 --> 00:27:11.480
-You don't know that.
-I do.

382
00:27:12.800 --> 00:27:14.760
Once he liberates
these lands from the Boltons.

383
00:27:14.920 --> 00:27:17.120
he'll rally your father's
bannermen to his cause.

384
00:27:17.280 --> 00:27:19.080
With the North behind him.

385
00:27:19.240 --> 00:27:21.520
Stannis can finally take
the Iron Throne.

386
00:27:21.680 --> 00:27:24.160
You think he'll
defeat the Boltons?

387
00:27:24.320 --> 00:27:25.800
He has a larger army.

388
00:27:25.960 --> 00:27:28.400
He's the finest military
commander in Westeros.

389
00:27:28.560 --> 00:27:31.800
A betting man would put
his money on Stannis.

390
00:27:31.960 --> 00:27:34.200
As it happens.
I am a betting man.

391
00:27:35.680 --> 00:27:37.280
And if you're right?

392
00:27:37.440 --> 00:27:39.320
Stannis takes Winterfell.

393
00:27:39.480 --> 00:27:42.240
he rescues you from the most despised
family in the North.

394
00:27:42.400 --> 00:27:45.320
Grateful for your late father's
courageous support of his claim.

395
00:27:45.480 --> 00:27:47.760
he names you
Wardeness of the North.

396
00:27:47.920 --> 00:27:50.080
But I--

397
00:27:50.240 --> 00:27:51.640
I wouldn't--

398
00:27:51.800 --> 00:27:53.240
Wardeness of the North?

399
00:27:53.400 --> 00:27:55.920
You are the last
surviving Stark.

400
00:27:56.080 --> 00:27:58.880
-He needs you.
-And what if you're wrong?

401
00:27:59.040 --> 00:28:00.680
What if Stannis never
attacks Winterfell?

402
00:28:00.840 --> 00:28:03.120
Or he does and the Boltons
defeat him?

403
00:28:03.280 --> 00:28:05.240
Then you will take
this Bolton boy. Ramsay.

404
00:28:05.400 --> 00:28:07.000
and make him yours.

405
00:28:07.160 --> 00:28:08.720
I don't know
how to do that.

406
00:28:08.880 --> 00:28:10.480
Of course you do.

407
00:28:10.640 --> 00:28:12.280
He's already
fallen for you.

408
00:28:12.440 --> 00:28:14.240
His father frightens me.

409
00:28:14.400 --> 00:28:17.600
He should.
He's a dangerous man.

410
00:28:17.760 --> 00:28:21.280
But even the most dangerous
men can be outmaneuvered.

411
00:28:21.440 --> 00:28:23.720
And you've learned
to maneuver from the very best.

412
00:28:25.960 --> 00:28:28.440
I'll return
before too long.

413
00:28:28.600 --> 00:28:31.160
You'll be strong
without me.

414
00:28:38.520 --> 00:28:40.440
The North will be yours.

415
00:28:41.840 --> 00:28:43.800
Do you believe me?

416
00:28:45.560 --> 00:28:48.800
I expect I'll be a married woman
by the time you return.

417
00:28:50.680 --> 00:28:52.160
( pats )

418
00:29:26.760 --> 00:29:28.920
( groans )

419
00:29:29.080 --> 00:29:31.360
( panting )

420
00:29:43.440 --> 00:29:45.720
( blade scraping )

421
00:29:50.040 --> 00:29:51.640
Breakfast.

422
00:29:55.480 --> 00:29:57.320
That would have been
a shit way to die.

423
00:29:57.480 --> 00:30:00.440
As far as I've seen.
they're all shit ways to die.

424
00:30:00.600 --> 00:30:03.720
Aye. but your lot have
to give the singers a good ending.

425
00:30:03.880 --> 00:30:06.120
I don't care what's sung about me
when I'm dead.

426
00:30:06.280 --> 00:30:08.160
No?

427
00:30:08.320 --> 00:30:10.800
Two knights off
to rescue a princess.

428
00:30:10.960 --> 00:30:12.600
Sounds like
a good song to me.

429
00:30:12.760 --> 00:30:14.840
Sounds like
all the rest.

430
00:30:17.520 --> 00:30:19.360
What about you?

431
00:30:19.520 --> 00:30:21.600
What shit way
would you choose?

432
00:30:22.960 --> 00:30:25.840
In my own keep
drinking my own wine

433
00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:27.960
watching my sons
grovel for my fortune.

434
00:30:29.080 --> 00:30:31.360
How disappointing.

435
00:30:31.520 --> 00:30:34.400
I thought you'd have something
more exciting planned.

436
00:30:34.560 --> 00:30:36.680
I've had
an exciting life.

437
00:30:36.840 --> 00:30:38.640
I want my death
to be boring.

438
00:30:40.280 --> 00:30:42.080
How do you
want to go?

439
00:30:42.240 --> 00:30:44.400
In the arms
of the woman I love.

440
00:30:47.640 --> 00:30:49.920
She want the same thing?

441
00:30:54.920 --> 00:30:56.360
Let's go.

442
00:31:05.840 --> 00:31:07.800
The captain of that ship--

443
00:31:07.960 --> 00:31:09.320
what was he. Braavosi?

444
00:31:09.480 --> 00:31:11.040
Pentoshi.

445
00:31:11.200 --> 00:31:12.600
And he's headed
to Oldtown?

446
00:31:12.760 --> 00:31:14.560
As I said.
Why?

447
00:31:14.720 --> 00:31:17.240
What's to stop him from
docking down the coast

448
00:31:17.400 --> 00:31:19.800
and telling the locals
that Jaime Lannister is in Dorne?

449
00:31:19.960 --> 00:31:21.800
A bag of gold.

450
00:31:21.960 --> 00:31:23.520
I'm not sure
you understand

451
00:31:23.680 --> 00:31:25.960
how much people hate your family
in this part of the world.

452
00:31:26.120 --> 00:31:27.680
It was a heavy bag.

453
00:31:27.840 --> 00:31:30.600
And I bet he swore all
kinds of oaths to get it.

454
00:31:30.760 --> 00:31:32.640
But you won't be around
if he breaks 'em.

455
00:31:32.800 --> 00:31:35.200
-( horse neighs )
-( hoofbeats )

456
00:31:42.040 --> 00:31:44.800
-Bronn: How many you count?
-Four.

457
00:31:44.960 --> 00:31:46.440
How many do you think
you can take?

458
00:31:46.600 --> 00:31:48.440
One if he's slow.

459
00:31:52.200 --> 00:31:53.720
Halt!

460
00:31:53.880 --> 00:31:55.680
Over the hill.

461
00:31:57.400 --> 00:31:59.400
Fucked in the ass.

462
00:32:03.400 --> 00:32:04.920
Hyah!

463
00:32:08.720 --> 00:32:10.880
Morning. lads.

464
00:32:11.040 --> 00:32:12.880
Glad we found you.

465
00:32:13.040 --> 00:32:14.360
Who are you?

466
00:32:14.520 --> 00:32:16.280
Cooper.

467
00:32:16.440 --> 00:32:18.480
This is Darnell.

468
00:32:18.640 --> 00:32:21.520
-You're from King's Landing.
-Accent gave me away?

469
00:32:22.720 --> 00:32:24.960
Flea Bottom.
whelped and whipped.

470
00:32:25.120 --> 00:32:26.640
Why are you here?

471
00:32:26.800 --> 00:32:28.440
Our ship capsized
in the night.

472
00:32:28.600 --> 00:32:32.440
We managed to swim ashore.
It was a near thing. really.

473
00:32:32.600 --> 00:32:34.920
Thought the sharks
would get us.

474
00:32:35.080 --> 00:32:37.760
There are no sharks
in Dorne.

475
00:32:39.080 --> 00:32:42.080
Could have sworn
those were shark fins.

476
00:32:42.240 --> 00:32:43.920
Dolphins. maybe.

477
00:32:45.600 --> 00:32:47.080
Throw your swords
in the sand.

478
00:32:47.240 --> 00:32:49.640
Boys. there's
no need for this.

479
00:32:49.800 --> 00:32:52.080
Just point us
in the right direction.

480
00:32:52.240 --> 00:32:53.720
we'll find our way home.

481
00:32:53.880 --> 00:32:56.080
Swords in the sand now.

482
00:33:06.000 --> 00:33:07.320
( grunts )

483
00:33:15.240 --> 00:33:17.320
Hyah! Hyah!

484
00:33:18.640 --> 00:33:20.720
( horse neighs )

485
00:33:22.760 --> 00:33:24.400
That one should
be slow enough.

486
00:33:30.040 --> 00:33:31.640
( shouts )

487
00:34:00.960 --> 00:34:02.880
( shouts )

488
00:34:12.000 --> 00:34:14.040
( grunts )

489
00:34:16.320 --> 00:34:17.800
Bronn:
Nice move.

490
00:34:19.120 --> 00:34:21.000
Luck.

491
00:34:21.160 --> 00:34:23.120
You had
a wonderful teacher.

492
00:34:36.040 --> 00:34:39.160
Always wanted
a Dornish stallion.

493
00:34:39.320 --> 00:34:42.400
Beasts can run
a day and night without tiring.

494
00:34:42.560 --> 00:34:44.240
We'll ride
to the Water Gardens

495
00:34:44.400 --> 00:34:45.920
with a nice breeze
in our faces.

496
00:34:46.080 --> 00:34:47.440
First we need
to bury these bodies.

497
00:34:48.520 --> 00:34:49.840
Birds have
to eat. too.

498
00:34:50.000 --> 00:34:52.160
Corpses raise questions.
Questions raise armies.

499
00:34:52.320 --> 00:34:54.520
We're not here
to start a war.

500
00:34:54.680 --> 00:34:57.240
Do you know how long
it'll take us to dig all those holes?

501
00:34:57.400 --> 00:35:00.280
I can't dig very well
with one hand.

502
00:35:00.440 --> 00:35:02.040
Not at all. really.

503
00:35:31.880 --> 00:35:33.480
Mama.

504
00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:40.400
Nym. Obara.

505
00:35:40.560 --> 00:35:42.360
Will it be war?

506
00:35:42.520 --> 00:35:44.880
Prince Doran will weep
for your father. but nothing else.

507
00:35:45.040 --> 00:35:47.080
We must avenge
Oberyn ourselves.

508
00:35:47.240 --> 00:35:50.360
Without Doran. we have no army
to march against the Lannisters.

509
00:35:50.520 --> 00:35:53.080
We don't need an army
to start a war.

510
00:35:53.240 --> 00:35:56.680
Queen Cersei loves
her children.

511
00:35:56.840 --> 00:35:58.560
And we have one of them.

512
00:35:58.720 --> 00:36:00.440
You may have a problem.

513
00:36:05.000 --> 00:36:06.640
( groaning )

514
00:36:06.800 --> 00:36:08.600
A ship's captain who found me in
Planky Town

515
00:36:08.760 --> 00:36:10.280
claiming he had
information to sell.

516
00:36:10.440 --> 00:36:14.040
He told me he smuggled
Jaime Lannister into Dorne.

517
00:36:15.320 --> 00:36:17.360
He's come for Myrcella.

518
00:36:18.560 --> 00:36:20.120
If he gets to her
before we do.

519
00:36:20.280 --> 00:36:22.880
we lose our only chance
for revenge.

520
00:36:23.040 --> 00:36:26.040
You must choose.

521
00:36:26.200 --> 00:36:27.880
Doran's way and peace.

522
00:36:28.040 --> 00:36:30.600
or my way and war.

523
00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:37.600
-I'm with you always.
-Nym?

524
00:36:41.680 --> 00:36:43.880
Obara?

525
00:36:44.040 --> 00:36:47.560
When I was a child.
Oberyn came to take me to court.

526
00:36:47.720 --> 00:36:49.320
I had never seen
this man.

527
00:36:49.480 --> 00:36:51.720
and yet he called
himself my father.

528
00:36:51.880 --> 00:36:56.280
My mother wept. said I was too young
and a girl.

529
00:36:58.760 --> 00:37:01.560
Oberyn tossed his spear
at my feet and said.

530
00:37:01.720 --> 00:37:04.360
"Girl or boy.
we fight our battles.

531
00:37:04.520 --> 00:37:07.600
but the gods let us
choose our weapons."

532
00:37:07.760 --> 00:37:10.160
My father pointed
to the spear

533
00:37:10.320 --> 00:37:12.080
and then
to my mother's tears.

534
00:37:14.680 --> 00:37:16.000
( grunts )

535
00:37:19.480 --> 00:37:21.640
I made my choice
long ago.

536
00:37:23.800 --> 00:37:26.840
( Tyrion muffled )
Will you untie me?

537
00:37:27.000 --> 00:37:29.680
( muffled )
Will you please untie me?

538
00:37:29.840 --> 00:37:31.720
( muffled groan )
Will you please?

539
00:37:33.840 --> 00:37:38.400
( muffled singing )

540
00:37:53.800 --> 00:37:55.400
Thank you.

541
00:38:03.280 --> 00:38:06.360
-Who are you?
-Your captor.

542
00:38:08.600 --> 00:38:10.200
Do you have wine?

543
00:38:10.360 --> 00:38:12.120
No.

544
00:38:12.280 --> 00:38:13.960
Can't sleep
without wine.

545
00:38:14.120 --> 00:38:16.000
Then stay awake.

546
00:38:21.400 --> 00:38:22.960
You're going
the wrong way.

547
00:38:24.440 --> 00:38:26.720
My sister
is in Westeros.

548
00:38:26.880 --> 00:38:29.440
Westeros is west.

549
00:38:29.600 --> 00:38:31.000
We're heading east.

550
00:38:31.160 --> 00:38:33.200
I'm not taking you
to your sister.

551
00:38:34.880 --> 00:38:36.960
You said you were
taking me to the queen.

552
00:38:37.120 --> 00:38:40.040
I am.
Queen Daenerys Targaryen.

553
00:38:40.200 --> 00:38:41.720
She's the queen I serve.

554
00:38:41.880 --> 00:38:44.240
( laughing )

555
00:38:48.080 --> 00:38:51.240
What a waste
of a good kidnapping.

556
00:38:51.400 --> 00:38:53.760
It so happens
I was heading there myself.

557
00:38:53.920 --> 00:38:55.880
What business would you
have with the queen?

558
00:38:56.040 --> 00:38:59.240
Gold and glory.
Oh. and hate.

559
00:38:59.400 --> 00:39:01.800
If you'd ever met my sister.
you'd understand.

560
00:39:03.120 --> 00:39:06.400
So. now that it's clear
we are on the same side...

561
00:39:16.000 --> 00:39:19.000
A highborn knight
from the North of Westeros

562
00:39:19.160 --> 00:39:21.360
down on his luck
in Essos.

563
00:39:21.520 --> 00:39:25.200
Dragon epaulets.
bear sigil breastplate.

564
00:39:26.640 --> 00:39:28.600
You're Jorah Mormont.

565
00:39:28.760 --> 00:39:31.320
I have to ask.

566
00:39:31.480 --> 00:39:33.480
How exactly were you
serving your queen

567
00:39:33.640 --> 00:39:36.080
in a whorehouse
half a world away?

568
00:39:36.240 --> 00:39:38.600
Is it possible
that you were running?

569
00:39:38.760 --> 00:39:41.120
Why would you be running?

570
00:39:41.280 --> 00:39:43.240
And why would she
have sent you away?

571
00:39:43.400 --> 00:39:46.320
Oh. wait.

572
00:39:46.480 --> 00:39:49.560
You were spying
on her. weren't you?

573
00:39:49.720 --> 00:39:51.200
It's all coming
back to me.

574
00:39:51.360 --> 00:39:53.480
I was drunk through
most of the small council meetings.

575
00:39:53.640 --> 00:39:55.160
but it's all coming back.

576
00:39:55.320 --> 00:39:58.880
You passed notes
to Varys's little birds.

577
00:39:59.040 --> 00:40:02.040
She found out.
didn't she?

578
00:40:02.200 --> 00:40:05.320
Found out and exiled you.

579
00:40:05.480 --> 00:40:09.880
Now you hope to win back
her favor with a gift.

580
00:40:10.040 --> 00:40:12.080
Risky scheme.

581
00:40:12.240 --> 00:40:14.600
One might
even say desperate.

582
00:40:16.160 --> 00:40:19.320
You think Daenerys
will execute me and pardon you?

583
00:40:20.840 --> 00:40:22.960
I'd say the reverse
is just as likely.

584
00:40:41.080 --> 00:40:43.440
( bird screeches )

585
00:40:43.600 --> 00:40:46.120
Everyone looks happy
enough from up here.

586
00:40:47.480 --> 00:40:49.880
-( laughs )
-What?

587
00:40:50.040 --> 00:40:51.680
I was thinking about
all the times your brother

588
00:40:51.840 --> 00:40:53.760
made me go with him
down from the Red Keep

589
00:40:53.920 --> 00:40:55.440
into the streets
of King's Landing.

590
00:40:55.600 --> 00:40:58.000
-Why?
-He liked to walk among the people.

591
00:40:58.160 --> 00:41:00.160
He liked to sing to them.

592
00:41:00.320 --> 00:41:01.680
He sang to them?

593
00:41:01.840 --> 00:41:03.680
-Yes.
-( laughs )

594
00:41:03.840 --> 00:41:05.920
Rhaegar would pick
a spot on the Hook

595
00:41:06.080 --> 00:41:08.880
or the Street of Seeds
and then he'd sing.

596
00:41:09.040 --> 00:41:10.360
Just like all
the other minstrels.

597
00:41:10.520 --> 00:41:13.240
-And what did you do?
-I made sure no one killed him.

598
00:41:13.400 --> 00:41:16.160
And I collected
the money.

599
00:41:16.320 --> 00:41:18.440
What? He liked to see
how much he could make.

600
00:41:18.600 --> 00:41:20.400
-He was good?
-He was very good.

601
00:41:20.560 --> 00:41:22.000
Viserys never told you?

602
00:41:22.160 --> 00:41:25.040
He told me Rhaegar
was good at killing people.

603
00:41:25.200 --> 00:41:27.880
Rhaegar never liked killing.
He loved singing.

604
00:41:28.040 --> 00:41:29.960
And what did you do
with the money?

605
00:41:30.120 --> 00:41:33.040
Well. one time. he gave it to
the next minstrel down the street.

606
00:41:33.200 --> 00:41:35.520
One time. he gave it
to an orphanage in Flea Bottom.

607
00:41:35.680 --> 00:41:39.120
One time. we got
horribly drunk.

608
00:41:39.280 --> 00:41:40.920
( laughs )

609
00:41:41.080 --> 00:41:43.040
Your Grace.

610
00:41:43.200 --> 00:41:46.600
Hizdahr is here. waiting
in the audience chamber.

611
00:41:46.760 --> 00:41:48.320
How many others
are there?

612
00:41:48.480 --> 00:41:51.240
50? 100?

613
00:41:51.400 --> 00:41:53.080
Will you be joining us.
Ser Barristan?

614
00:41:53.240 --> 00:41:56.760
I think I can protect you
from Hizdahr zo Loraq.

615
00:41:56.920 --> 00:41:59.200
I think I can protect me
from Hizdahr zo Loraq.

616
00:42:00.320 --> 00:42:01.720
Go. Ser Barristan.

617
00:42:01.880 --> 00:42:05.400
-Sing a song for me.
-Your Grace.

618
00:42:10.280 --> 00:42:13.480
All men must die.
but not all can die in glory.

619
00:42:13.640 --> 00:42:15.520
-Glory?
-Why else do men fight?

620
00:42:15.680 --> 00:42:17.720
Why did your ancestors
cross the Narrow Sea

621
00:42:17.880 --> 00:42:21.680
and conquer the Seven Kingdoms?
So their names would live on.

622
00:42:21.840 --> 00:42:23.280
Those who find victory
in the fighting pits

623
00:42:23.440 --> 00:42:26.480
will never become kings.
but their names will live on.

624
00:42:26.640 --> 00:42:28.280
It's the best chance
they'll ever have.

625
00:42:28.440 --> 00:42:29.960
Is that what
you used to tell men

626
00:42:30.120 --> 00:42:32.680
before you set them
to butchering each other for sport?

627
00:42:32.840 --> 00:42:35.400
Your Grace. today is the traditional
start of the fighting season.

628
00:42:35.560 --> 00:42:37.160
I do not recognize
this tradition.

629
00:42:37.320 --> 00:42:40.240
Traditions are the only thing
that will hold this city.

630
00:42:40.400 --> 00:42:41.800
your city. together.

631
00:42:43.440 --> 00:42:45.680
Without them.
former slaves and former masters

632
00:42:45.840 --> 00:42:47.160
have nothing
in common.

633
00:42:48.840 --> 00:42:53.400
Nothing but centuries
of mistrust and resentment.

634
00:42:53.560 --> 00:42:56.760
I can't promise this is the answer
to all our problems.

635
00:42:56.920 --> 00:42:59.040
but it's a start.

636
00:43:05.560 --> 00:43:07.280
( laughing )

637
00:43:09.840 --> 00:43:11.320
( gurgling )

638
00:43:11.480 --> 00:43:13.840
-( grunts )
-( people shouting )

639
00:43:22.960 --> 00:43:25.840
( people shouting )

640
00:43:31.080 --> 00:43:33.400
( crying )

641
00:43:33.560 --> 00:43:35.480
( speaking Valyrian )

642
00:44:02.320 --> 00:44:04.000
( shouting )

643
00:44:26.720 --> 00:44:28.280
( shouts )

644
00:44:38.000 --> 00:44:39.320
( groans )

645
00:44:44.480 --> 00:44:47.280
( alarm bell ringing )

646
00:44:47.440 --> 00:44:49.520
( men shouting )

647
00:45:05.520 --> 00:45:06.840
( screams )

648
00:45:16.560 --> 00:45:18.240
( groans )

649
00:45:43.840 --> 00:45:46.360
( panting )

650
00:45:46.520 --> 00:45:49.000
( man shouts )

651
00:45:49.160 --> 00:45:51.040
( grunts )

652
00:46:20.080 --> 00:46:21.480
( grunts )

653
00:46:33.920 --> 00:46:35.680
( screams )

654
00:46:38.400 --> 00:46:40.160
( grunts )

655
00:46:52.200 --> 00:46:54.360
( alarm bell
continues ringing )

656
00:47:03.720 --> 00:47:06.560
( music playing )
